Build 1.2.5 - 2026-08-14 - THE TWO DEFECTS REPORTED ON 1086, PLUS 1086's BATCH
Cut from main @ f8c1985. typecheck clean, 1345 tests green, build clean,
security audit 0 critical / 0 high.

⚠ 1086 WAS HALTED IN PLAY. Do not ship 1086. This build replaces it and
carries everything 1086 carried.

FIXED IN THIS BUILD - the two things reported on 1086

- "+ CREATE" IS IN THE LEFT CORNER, AND IT IS AN ICON WITH NO CAPTION.
  On 1086 it sat in the MIDDLE of the top bar, on top of the centred
  wordmark. The cause was layout, not a coordinate: the bar is
  `justify-between`, and in the app the logo <Link> collapses to ZERO width
  because its image and its wordmark are both `hidden lg:*`. Three flex
  children with a zero-width first one spread as [nothing] ... [+ Create]
  ... [actions], which parks the button in the centre. The logo and the
  button now share ONE wrapper, so they are ONE flex item and sit at the
  left edge. Measured in a headless render before shipping: the button
  starts 24px from the bar edge and ends at 61px; the wordmark starts at
  69px. On 1086 it started at 125px and overlapped. The "Create" caption is
  gone - the name is on aria-label, and the box is 36px so the tap target
  stays finger-sized without it.

- A VERIFIED TAGGED MEMBER NOW SHOWS THE BLUE TICK. So does a verified
  AUTHOR, which was the same bug.
  Checked against production first: the badge row exists, RLS is "Anyone can
  view badges" USING (true), and a real anonymous REST call returns it. The
  data was always reachable and the component was always correct - what
  failed was the lookup between them. The tick came from a SECOND, per-name
  request fired at render time, while the query that built that very line had
  already fetched those profiles WITH their badges and thrown the badges
  away. Author and tagged name go through the identical path, so this was
  never tagged-only: `author_badges` has been computed by every feed, wall
  and hashtag query for months and no caller ever read it.
  Badges now travel WITH the post - the same correction as the author-name
  fix. "Name visible, badge missing" is no longer a state this app can be in.

ALSO IN THIS BUILD - everything from 1086

- The feed no longer runs out of memory on a long scroll. Cards unmount about
  two screens away; 100 mounted cards was the crash on a mid-range Android.
- The blurred backdrop no longer downloads the 2560px original (14.7 MB of
  RAM once decoded), and the LQIP no longer falls through to it.
- React Query stops retaining every page ever fetched (maxPages: 5).
- Author names and avatars arrive WITH the post - get_broadcast_feed returns
  15 columns instead of 11.
- Realtime traffic halved (9 bindings -> 5) and counters can no longer drift:
  one writer per field, absolute totals from `posts`.
- A weak signal no longer looks like an empty app - the feed and drafts throw
  and retry instead of caching an empty success as truth.
- Typing in a comment edit no longer reverses the text.
- Blue tick shows with the name everywhere, including "with X".

BUILD SYSTEM
All 11 Capacitor packages pinned, with a step that FAILS the build if a pin
did not take. Node 22.

WHAT IS *NOT* IN THIS BUILD - do not expect it
- The Instagram-style in-app photo picker. Picker screens are unchanged.
- The image derivative pipeline. Phones still download originals.
- Resumable / chunked uploads.

BEFORE PROMOTING TO PRODUCTION
Sideload the debug APK this run produces and check, in this order:
  1. The + Create icon is in the LEFT corner and does not touch the wordmark.
  2. A verified member shows the blue tick - as the post author AND as a
     tagged name in "with X".
  3. Scroll the feed hard and back: no blank cards, no scroll jump.
  4. Type and edit a comment; categories and contributor score still render.
  5. Like a post - the count moves by exactly one.
Then promote the AAB.
